Subject: [PATCH 6/7] patch 0006: parallelize refresh file hashing

The Refresh() function walked every file sequentially and hashed it.
On a 300-mod pack this is the main bottleneck.

Extract computeFileHash() as a pure, goroutine-safe function.
Refactor updateFile() to use it (preserves existing callers).
Replace the sequential loop in Refresh() with a bounded goroutine
pool that hashes all files in parallel, then applies the results to
the index map serially — no mutex needed on IndexFiles.

The mpb progress bar is goroutine-safe; Increment() calls from
goroutines are fine.

